-- ============================================================
--  NexusLib v3.1.3  |  Roblox UI Library
--
--  Drop-in replacement for v3.0 / v2.5: every older call still works.
--  Everything new is opt-in (window / element options).
--
--  3.1.3 FIXES
--   * The real dropdown / combo box bug: the pointer position (GetMouseLocation,
--     top bar included) and the window's AbsolutePosition were in different
--     spaces when the ScreenGui didn't actually ignore the top-bar inset, so
--     "is the click inside the list?" was ~58 px off: lists closed before a
--     row's click landed (3.1.0-3.1.1) or picked the wrong row / closed at
--     once (3.1.2). Lists no longer use coordinates at all: each part of a
--     list reports presses through its own InputBegan (engine hit test), and
--     an outside press only closes it a frame later if nothing inside was hit.
--     Rows pick on press (click as a fallback); hover is MouseEnter/Leave.
--   * PointerPos (keybind cancel, floating dropdowns) corrects for the inset.
--
--  3.1.2 (superseded by 3.1.3)
--   * Dropdown / combo box rows couldn't be picked in some executors (the
--     row's click event never arrived). Rows are now picked on press by
--     hit-testing the pointer (UserInputService), hover the same way.
--
--  3.1.1 FIXES
--   * ComboBox: clicking a row could close the list before the click landed
--     (it relied on MouseEnter/MouseLeave, which Roblox doesn't fire
--     reliably) - now checks whether the pointer is over the list.
--   * Picking a ComboBox row no longer rebuilds the list mid-click.
--   * Global search results covered the pages (blocking every dropdown /
--     button) until the box was emptied by hand - picking a tab clears them.
--   * Opening a second inline list while one was open made both scroll the
--     page at once (jumpy); only the last one scrolls back now.
--
--  NEW IN 3.1
--   * Search (CreateWindow{Search = true}):
--       - a filter bar at the top of every tab (Tab option NoSearch = true
--         to skip one). Hides elements / sections that don't contain all
--         typed words; a matching section title keeps the whole section.
--       - a global search box at the top of the sidebar: results as
--         "Tab > Section > Feature"; clicking one opens the tab, filters it
--         to that feature and scrolls to it.
--       - sections / elements created later are searchable too;
--         Section option NoSearch = true leaves a section out.
--   * Config (automatic): every Toggle / Slider / Keybind / Dropdown /
--     ColorPicker is registered as "Tab/Section/Name" (Textbox with
--     Save = true). Opt out with NoSave = true on the element or section.
--       Win:GetConfig() -> table      Win:LoadConfig(t)  (fires callbacks
--       only for values that change, in creation order)
--       Win:ExportConfig(t?, meta?) -> JSON text (+ clipboard)
--       Win:ImportConfig(text) -> table, meta
--       Win:SaveConfig(name) / LoadConfigFile(name) / ListConfigs() /
--       DeleteConfig(name)   (files in opts.ConfigFolder)
--   * Inline dropdowns (CreateWindow{InlineDropdowns = true} or
--     Dropdown{Inline = true}): the list opens inside the section, multi
--     select stays open, the tab scrolls to show it and back.
--   * ComboBox element: type a name or pick one from a list (Items may be a
--     function), Highlight(item), OnOpen, EmptyText, :SetStatus().
--   * Slider AllowOverflow = true: typing a value above Max stretches the
--     slider instead of clamping (Max is only the drag range).
--   * Toggle Keybind = "F" (or true for unbound): a key button on the toggle
--     row; the key flips the toggle. KeybindNotify / window option
--     KeybindNotifications show an Enabled / Disabled notification.
--     Saved in the config as "Name [Key]".
--   * Toggle Module = true / "Label": Win:GetActiveModules() lists the ones
--     that are on; NexusLib:CreateModList{} draws them as a draggable
--     overlay (or any list from a Provider function).
--   * Escape and the Roblox menu close every open list / popup
--     (NexusLib:CloseAll, NexusLib:AddPopupCloser(fn) for your own).
--   * The tab sidebar scrolls when there are more tabs than fit.
--   * Section: :SetOrder(n) / opts.Order (position on the page).
--   * Win:GetTab(name), Tab:GetSections(), Element._path (config key).
--
--  ---- 3.0 notes ----
--  Drop-in replacement for v2.5: every v2.5 call still works.
--
--  FIXES
--   * Slider sent unrounded values to callbacks (Precision was only
--     applied to the display). Values now snap to Precision/Increment
--     and the callback only fires when the value actually changes.
--   * Slider/colour picker/drag now work with touch input.
--   * Closing the window left every keybind/slider/drag listener
--     connected. Close now runs OnClose callbacks and fully destroys
--     the library (DestroyOnClose = false to keep the old behaviour).
--   * Re-executing destroyed the old GUI but not its connections.
--   * Glyphs that render as squares (close, minimize, arrows) are now
--     drawn from frames.
--   * Sections/accordions animated in 10 fixed task.wait steps and
--     resized one frame late. Now eased per-frame and follow content
--     changes instantly; nested accordions no longer need delays.
--   * Colour picker fired its callback on creation.
--   * Label text over one line was clipped (fixed 26px height).
--   * Notifications overlapped once earlier ones left.
--   * Prompt buttons appeared in random order (pairs()).
--   * Dropdown list stayed floating in place when the page scrolled
--     or the window moved; SetItems didn't refresh an open list.
--   * Keybind listening could get stuck if another keybind was
--     clicked; clicking elsewhere now cancels listening.
--   * Toggle pill reverted to its initial colour on theme change.
--   * LayoutOrder was computed from child counts (duplicates after
--     removals). Now uses counters.
--   * Accordion elements lacked features section elements had
--     (Precision, Description, Dropdown, Textbox...). Both now share
--     one element builder.
--
--  NEW
--   * Notify: rounded accent edge + progress bar that follow the
--     corners, stacking that reflows, click to dismiss. Returns handle.
--   * Dropdown: Multi = true (checkbox list), Items may be a function,
--     Search, :Refresh(), :Open(), :Close().
--   * Keybind: ReleaseCallback (fires on key release) for hold keys.
--   * Every element: :Destroy(), :SetVisible(bool).
--   * Button: :Set(text) / :SetText(text), :SetDescription(text).
--   * Section: :Destroy(), :SetVisible(), :Collapse(), :Expand(),
--     :EnableRename(callback), sopts.Collapsed.
--   * Window: :OnClose(fn), :SetVisible(bool), :SelectTab(name),
--     :SetTitle(text); opts.OnClose, opts.DestroyOnClose.
--   * NexusLib:OnUnload(fn) runs when the library is destroyed.
--   * Tab: :Select(). Prompt accepts an ordered list of buttons.
-- ============================================================

